    {
      "turn": 6,
      "doctor_question": "Have these attention and organization problems caused serious problems in your daily life?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, I suppose they have. At the shop, it's been a real mess lately. I mean, we've had late orders because I just lose track of which tickets go with which garments, especially when it gets busy and Gary is yelling from the back. And the billing—oh, don't get me started on the billing. I've gotten the numbers jumbled up more times than I can count, and it leads to these incredibly tense moments with the customers. You know, Mrs. Higgins came in last Tuesday, and I accidentally charged her for someone else's suede jacket cleaning, and she was just furious, understandably so, but it just made my stomach tie in knots. And the other girls at the counter get so frustrated with me when they have to fix my mistakes. It’s just awful. \n\nAnd it’s not just work, either. At church, I used to love helping out with the potluck committee and organizing the spring bazaar. I really did. But I had to step back from leading the planning this year. I was supposed to be in charge of coordinating the volunteers, and I kept forgetting to call people back, or I'd lose the sign-up sheet, and people were getting so annoyed with me. Pastor Dave was very sweet about it, but I could tell he was exasperated when the tablecloths didn't show up on time because I forgot to confirm the rental. It just feels like I'm letting everyone down, everywhere I go, because I just can't seem to keep it all straight in my head.",
